#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166520 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166904 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dddc6159-ac4a-50ac-a366-08a4b809c925" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "c5e60742-2571-5100-96be-a7578e6dda07" :question/math-academy-id "e-21540" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/ea/ea1c45c30bc57d8f04e7bba3e30a33884899fffd0fb712032595ee742a72704c.svg)\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/c3/c3be7834b927a4b8ba684899ee4e617a752ca3f5e09f10a320552fc7f497fb32.svg)\nFind the general solution of the system." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\mathbf{x}_c(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/6c/6c0f164deb5815fc1c79e3dd724b6725168213938a81089867f4343cb4f05974.svg)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n![](images/5d/5dc5186154c40546a088db1890991e83c6f594d0042866ae9b86cddb3f2d08d8.svg)\nwhere $a,b$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of $\\mathbf{x}_p$ with respect to $t$ gives\n![](images/fa/fad28fb44ef22f703cbc8bd6a07d7d35e4a77ffe4fb3cd0ec5fdd3b107317a1b.svg)\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute $\\mathbf{x}_p$ and $\\mathbf{x}'_p$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{7t}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 7\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a+b \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a+b-1 \\\\ b-3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1 &=7a \\\\ b-3 &=7b\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nb - 7b = 3\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nb = -\\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n3a - \\dfrac12 - 1 = 7a\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\na = -\\dfrac38.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n![](images/29/29dcb07dde2cdecb330fddb6168319527336ed7a217506727aa6c28241e32a4c.svg)\n\nAnd thus, the general solution is given by\n![](images/3e/3e1b5e881fb3c6d5688fd4978ed0fcc16aec5c6e105c11b919a6a9810762d698.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "6f03c3e2-26dc-5ef3-90d9-9b80feac1ad4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21541" :question/problem "![](images/19/192b8b3ce80dafb1a2db21822dad5b477cef90793305284210797cba32536a9f.svg)\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n![](images/55/55f17316cc2c0c5965b1d01598bceec9c2c472d6f6c949a099e65b778e6659e4.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n![](images/e6/e6793e6bbadc20520b14292e048050c850340a535d2ade61a84d5235884794fa.svg)\nwhere $c_1,c_2$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2.$ Substituting $t = 0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\ {e}^{0}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{0}^{2}-0+4 \\\\ -{0}^{2}+2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+4 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+4 &=6 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2 &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $c_1 = 2.$ From the second equation, we have $c_2 = -1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n![](images/bc/bcd9c686f0b6924614b0fadf4d86f7872f3fa33837aedfa0f89c15e9720a8f45.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of a Particular Solution for Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "a5c44ae4-e55b-512f-ac1c-46f62950c1f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21543" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/ee/ee9461106f5c5b7de1ab9871852a1dcc5042947b635ffe10aba17286dac7124a.svg)\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/90/906d3f915ddca1fae48aa190a0a84236a91b50d5760db43816b1b72f20a4c52c.svg)\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t),$ where $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution $\\mathbf{x}_p(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/97/9790c520e0752c38ac78a0b0266f7b6da292e4db16a353f34a902b587a4e688c.svg)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n![](images/3d/3db9994bc0cab42e973fae4fa0b6f94ce880aa052707d11826fe94f6f75095ad.svg)\nwhere $a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2$ are constants that are to be determined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166902 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51834713-edc2-5af3-a0dc-fb54ea4040c6" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs in Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "aabc0f35-fdfc-573a-8d86-ada823a380a4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21544" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+4{t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{1}(t)-{t}^{2}+5t+6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWrite the system of linear ODEs in matrix form." :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=(-2)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+4\\cdot {t}^{2}+1\\cdot t+(-2) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+0\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {t}^{2}+5\\cdot t+6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n![](images/4d/4dd9b46275644b83a7aa7ab9f9eaf14a8792442e07c4c4fd3a84a296f1fc2ccd.svg)\nwhere ![](images/96/96e96bf02a2ba8f46452e9ef33bcc6215b1b0696c4e1c6262c1400215857839a.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166904 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dddc6159-ac4a-50ac-a366-08a4b809c925" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "168093fa-9a63-55ce-a515-83e652a3a0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "168093fa-9a63-55ce-a515-83e652a3a0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530907} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea5b94c4-3306-5d49-855d-afe455c01aa5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164047} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68397710-f20c-5389-86e2-ff7174f9153b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68397710-f20c-5389-86e2-ff7174f9153b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531096} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c20aac8-15b9-5440-a48b-88962676fa1b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf7f020c-a5a0-5a03-9077-32253a6eed74" :question/math-academy-id "q-329074" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3/2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1/2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2t+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{1}-{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2t+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0t+{a}_{1} \\\\ 0t+{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}({a}_{1}+3{a}_{2})t+({b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}+1) \\\\ ({a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-2)t+({b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=0 \\\\ {a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-2=0 \\\\ {b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}+1={a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+1={a}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first two equations, we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\frac{3}{2},\\,{a}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting these into the third and fourth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-1,\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3/2 \\\\ -1/2\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1/2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "a4ab9790-c0c6-544a-a432-a8e9b94f465e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164057} {:answer-field/id #uuid "5015578f-4b52-5778-9835-73f1be57bda3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed0f8885-a11d-56da-9ae3-53426b16b759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed0f8885-a11d-56da-9ae3-53426b16b759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377129} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec277bb-302e-57c9-a307-da92df4f2811" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142b6bf7-f8fa-5432-81f9-086f88c7a36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "142b6bf7-f8fa-5432-81f9-086f88c7a36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377131} :answer-field/id #uuid "553a710f-e04f-5190-a3f2-c7b179687774" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7dfc036b-75fb-5496-8e88-28b92588d762" :question/math-academy-id "q-329265" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(0))\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(0)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-2(0)}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 2{c}_{1} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{2}=4.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166902 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51834713-edc2-5af3-a0dc-fb54ea4040c6" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5415ccef-2daa-5ccc-b623-0d5b2ef82a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5415ccef-2daa-5ccc-b623-0d5b2ef82a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531049} :answer-field/id #uuid "bebe506f-ae90-5464-86d9-105fa3166d25" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb9f1d94-613f-52d8-bed3-02b8cc0988ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9f1d94-613f-52d8-bed3-02b8cc0988ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531376} :answer-field/id #uuid "e43a570f-6bf7-5576-bdcc-b2771eef1231" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f90e41d-7567-5c70-89dd-5be89aa21d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f90e41d-7567-5c70-89dd-5be89aa21d85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530925} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1517c77-b060-5246-8e3c-5ac989fed945" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5a7fd14-822d-53dd-9386-a03cd4c41c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 175921